WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.210
Hydrogen burns in
oxygen to make water.

2
00:00:03.260 --> 00:00:07.630
Write it with one of each: a
hydrogen molecule, two atoms.

3
00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:10.390
An oxygen molecule, two atoms.

4
00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:14.470
A water molecule, two
hydrogens and one oxygen.

5
00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:15.710
Now count.

6
00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:19.590
Two oxygen atoms went in,
but only one came out.

7
00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:23.230
An atom has vanished,
and atoms can't vanish.

8
00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:25.950
The quick fix is to give
water a second oxygen.

9
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:29.290
But you're not allowed to
touch water's formula.

10
00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:30.270
Why not?

11
00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:33.370
And if you can't change
that, what can you change?

12
00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:36.910
In this mission, you'll read
formulae and count every atom in

13
00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:37.300
them.

14
00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:41.290
You'll balance equations, and
work out relative formula masses.

15
00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:45.470
Your mission: balance the
equation without changing water.
